From 96e94c7cca7f57c9fda3afbf27621e5b16ff4d5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:48:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban comment writer: LC_HERMES_AGENT marker
 survives `ssh <Mac> hermes kanban comment`

Two agent-written comments recorded writer_kind=human (replica 40715 on
t_01a1d3a625e2f2b8, 41612 on t_01a1d5199d20cf3f): an agent's terminal ran
`ssh <Mac> 'hermes kanban comment ...'`. Mac sshd accepts only LANG LC_*
(/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/100-macos.conf), so every HERMES_* marker is dropped,
the remote shell starts clean, and the ancestry walk (sshd-session and
launchd skipped as root's) ends human.

Fix: use the LC_ prefix stock OpenSSH already forwards and accepts on every
host (client `SendEnv LANG LC_*`, server `AcceptEnv LANG LC_*`). No sshd
edit, no sudo.

- kanban_comment_writer: LC_HERMES_AGENT joins AGENT_ENV_MARKERS (blank still
  means no marker). New helpers: ssh_agent_marker_value / stamp_ssh_agent_marker
  (the child's HERMES_SESSION_ID, else an inherited marker, else "1"; an unsafe
  value becomes "1") and marker_session: when the CLI has no HERMES_SESSION_ID,
  a session-id-shaped LC_HERMES_AGENT (hermes_state_ids shapes or
  local-<64 hex>) becomes writer_session; "1" names none. Docstring no longer
  lists `ssh <host> hermes kanban comment` as out of reach.
- Exported next to every HERMES_AGENT site:
  - terminal wrapper (BaseEnvironment._wrap_command, every backend):
    `export LC_HERMES_AGENT="${HERMES_SESSION_ID:-${LC_HERMES_AGENT:-1}}"`,
    and the snapshot dump unsets it like AI_AGENT/HERMES_AGENT (a shared
    snapshot would otherwise carry one session's id into another's commands);
  - local spawn factory (_finalize_child_env: build_subprocess_env scrubbed
    path, hermes_subprocess_env, _sanitize_subprocess_env), stamped after the
    session bridge so it names this child's session. The unscrubbed
    build_subprocess_env path stays byte-preserving (it inherits main()'s "1");
  - execute_code child (_build_child_env, after _bridge_session_identity);
  - Kanban worker env (dispatcher): "1" after dropping the mirrored session
    vars, so a worker never carries a previous gateway turn's session id;
  - main()/gateway entrypoints setdefault "1"; MCP stdio servers carry it.
- drop_agent_attribution drops it, so the Desktop GUI (and its terminal pane,
  a person's shell) never starts with it.

Unchanged: a person's shell sets no LC_HERMES_AGENT, so their ssh notes stay
human; `/kanban` typed in a composer stays human; a leaked marker only lowers
authority.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_cli_comment_writer.py,
test_kanban_worker_session_source.py): ancestor env with only
LC_HERMES_AGENT=<sid> -> agent with that writer_session; blank -> human;
person's ssh with LANG/LC_CTYPE only -> human; marker value rules; real-bash
wrapper export; snapshot exclusion; build_subprocess_env, execute_code child,
entrypoint, MCP and worker env carry it.
RED on origin/main: 18 failed, 48 passed. GREEN: 67 passed.
91 files importing the touched builders: 1701 passed (one byte-preservation
failure found and fixed by not stamping the unscrubbed path).
